# WHAT EVERY WORKTREE OF THIS REPOSITORY NEEDS, AND NONE OF THEM SHOULD BUILD ITSELF.
#
# The presence of this file is the declaration, in the same spirit as the four beside it:
# `richos/engine/mega-lander/create-teammate-worktree.sh` runs it, with the new worktree as
# the working directory, immediately after creating and seeding that worktree. It is never
# fatal — a worktree whose setup failed is a worktree that works and rebuilds more — and it
# is killed if it runs longer than two minutes, so a bad edit here cannot hang every spawn
# on the machine.
#
# This Mac holds many checkouts. A shared target directory let Cargo run another
# checkout's stale binary when the current source timestamps were older. Each
# physical Cargo workspace now keeps its own mutable output on the external SSD.
# Registry downloads remain shared. Repeated builds reuse that workspace's output.
#
# It is deliberately a SHELL SCRIPT and not a list of paths. What a repository needs per
# worktree is not one shape — today it is two symlinks, tomorrow it could be a generated
# file — and a config format invented for one caller becomes a second thing to keep true.
#
# Run it by hand in any checkout that predates this file:
#     bash .richos/worktree-setup

set -uo pipefail

# Private Cargo output under the configured cache root. Existing shared links
# are retargeted without deleting their artifacts. Real directories need --adopt.
bash richos/app/scripts/shared-build-cache.sh .

# Playwright needs nothing here. `richos/app/ui/tests/lib/harness.js` derives the main
# checkout's install from git at the moment it is needed, so a worktree carries no copy and
# no symlink of `node_modules` at all.
